                <formatted-text>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#d30000' fontsize='16'>How do Partial Orders impact </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#d30000' fontname='Tableau Bold' fontsize='16'>30d retention</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#d30000' fontsize='16'> and </run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#d30000' fontname='Tableau Bold' fontsize='16'># of Days to reorder</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#d30000' fontsize='16'>?</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000'>Assumption</run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000'>:</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000'>Æ </run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000'>In some markets &apos;sorry vouchers&apos; are issued following a trial partial order. In this context, we are assuming that if an order is placed using a voucher, it is likely due to this voucher issuance</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000'>Organic Return: </run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000'>Customer who placed the second order organically (without any voucher)</run>
                  <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                  <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000'>Voucher Return: </run>
                  <run fontcolor='#000000'>Customer who placed the second order with  voucher</run>
                </formatted-text>
